-- title:
--   Graded descent for a subalgebra with bijective base change
-- statement:
--   Let $S$ and $S'$ be commutative rings with $S'$ an $S$-algebra, and let $A'$ be a commutative ring that is both an $S$-algebra and an $S'$-algebra, compatibly (scalar tower $S \to S' \to A'$). Let $\mathcal A' : \mathbb N \to \mathrm{Submodule}\,S'\,A'$ be a grading making $A'$ a graded $S'$-algebra, and let $A$ be an $S$-subalgebra of $A'$. Assume (i) the $S'$-algebra map $S' \otimes_S A \to A'$ determined by the structure map $S' \to A'$ and the inclusion $A \hookrightarrow A'$ (these commute, $A'$ being commutative) is bijective, and (ii) for every $a \in A$ and every $n$, the $n$-th homogeneous component of $a$ with respect to $\mathcal A'$ again lies in $A$. Then there exist a family $\mathcal A : \mathbb N \to \mathrm{Submodule}\,S\,A$ together with a graded $S$-algebra structure on $A$ for $\mathcal A$, and a proof $h_{\mathcal A}$ that the inclusion carries $\mathcal A_n$ into $\mathcal A'_n$ for each $n$, such that: conversely every $a \in A$ whose image in $A'$ lies in $\mathcal A'_n$ lies in $\mathcal A_n$ (so $\mathcal A_n$ is exactly $A \cap \mathcal A'_n$); for each $n$ the $S$-linear map $\mathcal A_n \to \mathcal A'_n$ obtained by restricting the inclusion exhibits $\mathcal A'_n$ (with scalars restricted to $S$) as the base change along $S \to S'$ of $\mathcal A_n$, i.e. $S' \otimes_S \mathcal A_n \xrightarrow{\sim} \mathcal A'_n$; and the irrelevant homogeneous ideal of $\mathcal A'$ is contained in the ideal generated by the image of the irrelevant homogeneous ideal of $\mathcal A$ under the graded ring homomorphism induced by the inclusion $A \hookrightarrow A'$ with the degree bound $h_{\mathcal A}$, that is $A'_+ = A_+ A'$.
--
--   This is the descent statement for gradings: a subalgebra whose base change to $S'$ recovers $A'$ and which is stable under taking homogeneous components is itself graded, degreewise by base change, and carries the irrelevant ideal of $A'$. It is the commutative-algebra input for the construction of $\mathrm{Proj}$ of a descended graded algebra, and is used by [`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_descent_of_faithfullyFlat_of_cocycle`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.exists_descent_of_faithfullyFlat_of_cocycle).
